# VoiceTranscriber

A personal macOS app that shows a live English transcript of computer audio
or the microphone, answers questions about it during the session, and writes
study notes with Claude when the session ends.

- Design spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-05-voicetranscriber-design.md`
- Implementation plan: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-05-voicetranscriber.md`

## Prerequisites

- A Mac with Apple Silicon (M3/M4 or newer), macOS 14+
- Xcode 16+
- XcodeGen: `brew install xcodegen`
- An Apple ID added in Xcode → Settings → Accounts (the free "Personal Team"
  is enough). Signing with it keeps macOS privacy permissions across rebuilds.

## Run the tests

    cd Kit && swift test

`TranscriptCore` and `AssistantKit` also build and test on Linux; the
capture and session targets only exist on macOS.

## Run the app

    xcodegen generate && open VoiceTranscriber.xcodeproj

Select the `VoiceTranscriber` target → Signing & Capabilities → set Team to
your Personal Team (or set `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` in `project.yml`), then Run (⌘R).

## Design and credits

The interface uses a warm parchment palette (tokens in `App/Design/Theme.swift`): ink text,
hairline warm-gray borders, softly rounded corners, and one deep teal reserved for selected
states. A warm charcoal dark theme follows macOS by default; Settings → Appearance can force
Light or Dark.

The Start / Stop / Pause / Resume buttons adapt the "Skiper 25" micro-interaction from
[Skiper UI](https://gxuri.me) by @gurvinder-singh02 (springy padding on hover and press, a
five-bar waveform), used under its free license, which requires this attribution.
